A key where the question is asked
=================================

The model chip in the composer is where "which model?" gets asked, so it should be where that gets
answered. Every provider in it ran the same handler, which opened the providers page — so choosing
Ollama Cloud and being told "not configured" sent you to a second screen to paste a key and then walk
back to the first.

An unconfigured provider now opens a key dialog in place: the field, a link to where the key comes
from, and one button that saves it through the same `/api/quixi/providers/save` the provider settings
use, tests it, and lands in that provider's model list. Local providers are not asked for a key they
do not have — the dialog says so, probes the port, and reports what answered.

